      {
        "name": "value?",
        "type": "DateValue | null",
        "notes": "A civil date and nothing finer: `commit` narrows every value to year, month and day, whichever child reported it, so the grid and the field cannot report two shapes of the same date. The consequence, stated because it used to be stated the other way round: a `date-field` given a time `granularity` inside a picker does **not** keep its own time. The picker *controls* the field's value, so the narrowed date is handed straight back and the time segments are cleared on every commit. A picker is a day picker; a time belongs to a field standing on its own, and to the `time-field` presentation the spec defers.",
        "source": "date-picker.types.ts:100",
        "group": "value"
      },
